From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 02:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] drm/msm/dp: Send HDR static metadata on eDP

The Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x (X1E80100) ships a Samsung ATNA45DC02 OLED whose
EDID advertises a CTA-861 HDR Static Metadata block with SMPTE ST2084, and
the link already runs at 30bpp because msm_dp_mode.bpp is derived from
display_info.bpc. Ten-bit pixels therefore reach the panel today, but the
sink is never told to interpret them with a PQ transfer function: drm/msm
attaches no HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA property, so userspace cannot ask, and the
driver sends no HDR infoframe.

Attach HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA on eDP, pack the metadata userspace supplies as
a CTA-861 Dynamic Range and Mastering infoframe wrapped in an SDP, and write
it to the VSCEXT registers during link bring-up.

The infoframe and the existing YUV420 VSC SDP live in different register
blocks -- VSCEXT and GENERIC0 -- so they are independent and either, both or
neither may be enabled. msm_dp_panel_send_sdp() gains a base register
argument to serve both; the header packing is identical, only the
destination differs. The teardown already cleared GENERIC0 from both
stream-off paths and now clears VSCEXT too, so it is renamed to reflect
that it serves both.

Deliberately not signalled: BT.2020 colorimetry. DP's MISC0 cannot express
it for RGB, so it would need a VSC SDP alongside the infoframe with BIT(6)
of MISC1 set to tell the sink to stop reading MSA. The ATNA45DC02 blanks
when told that -- link training passes both phases and the stream comes up
at the correct rate, so the panel is refusing the description of the stream
rather than failing to sync. The DP colorspace property is therefore not
attached either, since it would be inert.

The infoframe is only written during link bring-up, so this relies on the
compositor performing a modeset when it changes the metadata.

Tested on a Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x, eDP-1 at 2944x1840@90, bpp 30, HBR2 x4,
playing HDR10 content under Hyprland.

Signed-off-by: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
